repository-code: "https://github.com/open-cora/cora"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-25"
keywords:
  - event-sourcing
  - domain-driven-design
  - bounded-contexts
  - hexagonal-architecture
  - beamline-automation
  - synchrotron
  - model-context-protocol
abstract: >-
  CORA is a development tree holding an event-sourced system of record and the
  clients that drive and report to it, each shipped as a repository of its own.
  The keeper models the experiment in bounded contexts over Postgres and
  publishes every operation twice, as an HTTP route and as an agent-protocol
  (MCP) tool, from a single handler. The conductor takes a dispatched procedure
  and walks it across a beamline, claiming the hardware each step names. The
  reporter relays what an acquisition engine did and says where the data
  landed. Nothing imports anything else: what binds them is prose and a pair of
  metadata keys that each side pins to literals in a test of its own.
